The revised reading correctly reports the stop, but **two serious issues remain before I can agree to the proposed test**. The clearest example is that the proposed change says to leave the final check unchanged, even though the independent audit found that parts of that same check can exclude facts the standard says to keep.

1. **Financing explanation — resolved.** [Results reading, lines 129–135](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:129) now distinguishes the three runs and says the new questions are not shown to have caused the two losses. The [independent reader, lines 7–10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/judgement-drops-reader.out:7) distinguishes missing evidence in one run from different reasoning in the other.

2. **Operating-margin explanation — resolved.** [Results reading, lines 136–139](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:136) identifies the roughly 66% figure used by both agreeing controls and says it is unknown whether that figure alone would change the split’s answers. The [independent reader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/judgement-drops-reader.out:12) reaches the same limited conclusion.

3. **Classification of the 64 misses — resolved.** [Results reading, lines 89–92](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:89) now reports 51 not written, six dropped by a check and seven present in other words, including the partnership the counting aid missed.

4. **What the probes establish — partly resolved.** [Results reading, lines 103–120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:103) now states the selected-sample, increased-unwanted-material and filing limitations. But [line 102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:99) still says the one-sentence contradiction “is not the cause.” Two sends on selected articles did not show an improvement; they do not rule out an effect elsewhere. The proposed edited text also remains untested.

5. **Prompt analysis and balanced test — partly resolved.** The full-request audit and second reader provide a substantially better foundation, and [the proposal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:158) uses three sends per version and checks both useful and unwanted material. The remaining problems are below.

6. **Six unclassified misses — resolved.** [Results reading, lines 42–50](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:42) adds three unclassified misses per arm, and [lines 23–25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:23) separately acknowledges the two control losses after handover.

7. **Missing results and breadth of the improvement — partly resolved.** [Results reading, lines 54–85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:54) adds the test breakdown, blind samples, ladders and dates; [lines 149–154](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:149) describes both useful and unwanted new questions and zero duplicates in both arms. One small reporting error remains: the listed definite reasons account for **16** of the 17 unwanted split questions, while the two unsure cases are listed alongside them. The arm keys remain outside the repository, so I cannot independently verify the per-arm assignment.

The **recommendation’s central idea is supported by the standard**: decide whether an analyst would note a fact before deciding which existing question receives it. The standard also says the relevant question need not already exist. The independent reader identifies the opening instruction as a narrower test and gives concrete examples of how the model applied it. This is a general issue, not a rule fitted to a particular company or article. The audit and the probe do **not** establish how much of the total loss that sentence caused.

**Serious finding 1 — the proposed edit leaves an identified conflict in place.** [Results reading, lines 158–162](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:158) says to align the background and figure instructions with the standard while keeping the final check unchanged. Yet the [independent audit, lines 50–57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/prompt-audit-b-reader.out:50) identifies those narrowing instructions in that check itself. The fact that production shares the check does not resolve the conflict.

**Fix:** reconcile each identified sentence with its exact standard boundary, including the final check, before deciding what stays. Preserve the distinction between old, already-known background and a newly reported fact about an existing arrangement. The audit also says the request dump lists field descriptions rather than the complete schema ([line 80](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/prompt-audit-b-reader.out:80)); inspect the complete schema before treating the whole-request audit as finished.

**Serious finding 2 — the proposed test does not yet define a balanced, refutable decision.** [Results reading, lines 164–166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:164) specifies random selection and three sends, but no sample size, coverage of cases the change could harm, prediction or failure boundary. A random subset could miss the cases where unwanted material or incorrect filing increases. Counting only gold-listed unwanted entries also leaves unmatched additions unjudged, although the probe showed those additions increased.

**Fix:** fix the sample and its coverage before sending; include cases where the current request succeeds as well as relevant missed and unwanted material, and have a blind reader assess a defined sample of unmatched additions and filing. Set the predicted result and failure conditions in advance, with fresh same-day controls. Use the small check first; under [AGENTS §7.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/AGENTS.md:315), a prompt change is accepted on the whole benchmark, not that subset. The stopped line must go to Alex before a registered test or window run.

I agree that the split should not be promoted and that the instruction to find useful facts is the strongest lead. I agree with the direction of the recommendation, but **not yet with the proposed unchanged final check or with the test as specified**. This was a read-only review; I did not change files or run model calls.

